<p id="mwBA"><i id="mwBQ"><b id="mwBg">Rediviva albifasciata</b></i> is a species of oil-collecting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Bee" title="Bee" id="mwBw">bee</a> in the <i id="mwCA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rediviva" title="Rediviva" id="mwCQ">Rediviva</a></i> genus and <i id="mwCg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Melittidae" title="Melittidae" id="mwCw">Melittidae</a></i> family endemic to South Africa.<sup about="#mwt7" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Steiner,_2002._1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Steiner, 2002."},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Steiner,_2002.-1"}}'><a href="./Rediviva_albifasciata#cite_note-Steiner,_2002.-1" id="mwDA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDw">]</span></span></a></sup> It is the smallest of all <i id="mwEA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rediviva" title="Rediviva" id="mwEQ">Rediviva</a></i> species.<sup about="#mwt8" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Steiner,_2002._1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Steiner, 2002."}}'><a href="./Rediviva_albifasciata#cite_note-Steiner,_2002.-1" id="mwEg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt4" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"rp","href":"./Template:Rp"},"params":{"p":{"wt":"59"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwFg"><span title="Page: 59"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>59<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwFw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Characteristics">Characteristics</h2>

<p id="mwGA">The distribution of <i id="mwGQ">Rediviva albifasciata</i> is strongly congruent with the distribution of the plant <i id="mwGg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Colpias_mollis" title="Colpias mollis" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGw">Colpias mollis</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt11" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Steiner,_2002._1-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Steiner, 2002."}}'><a href="./Rediviva_albifasciata#cite_note-Steiner,_2002.-1" id="mwHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt9" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"rp","href":"./Template:Rp"},"params":{"p":{"wt":"61"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwIA"><span title="Page: 61"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>61<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> Its size allows it to collect oil from <i id="mwIQ">C. mollis</i> flowers much more easily than other bees, such as <i id="mwIg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rediviva_bicava?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Rediviva bicava" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Rediviva bicava"]}}' id="mwIw">R. bicava</a></i> and <i id="mwJA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rediviva_parva?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Rediviva parva" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Rediviva parva"]}}' id="mwJQ">R. parva</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt12" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Steiner,_2002._1-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Steiner, 2002."}}'><a href="./Rediviva_albifasciata#cite_note-Steiner,_2002.-1" id="mwJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt10" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"rp","href":"./Template:Rp"},"params":{"p":{"wt":"59"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwKg"><span title="Page: 59"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>59<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

<p id="mwKw">The forelegs of <i id="mwLA">R. albifasciata</i> are covered in blade-like hairs ventrally that allow it to collect and rupture elaiophores from <i id="mwLQ">C. mollis.</i><sup about="#mwt15" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="./Rediviva_albifasciata#cite_note-2" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

